   "meta": {
    "application": "BambuStudio-02.07.01.62",
    "profile_title": "0.2mm layer, 6 walls, 15% infill",
    "profile_notes": "My kids loved the original sooo much I decided to go big or go home with this remix. All I did was split the parts up and fit them (reoriented the main body and the fins) on 4 separate plates then did a uniform scale of 185% for all pieces. This was printed on my P1S using Bambu Translucent Blue PLA without any failure. A permanent marker was used for the eyes. This guy glides a further distance. All thanks goes out to the original maker of this cool model for fun in the sun (above ground pool)! 30 July 2026: I've added a photo showing how acrylic permanent markers were used to customize the coloring to add a unique (subtle) touch for only a slighter ability to see the guy glide in the water; a single googly eye was added using JB Weld Clear Epoxy (also coated the outside of the googly eye for waterproof using the epoxy). I allowed both the acrylic marker and epoxy to dry/settle for more than 24 hours per the instructions. After MANY uses in the pool all unique touches remain the same as initially designed / painted. Highly recommend doing exactly what I did but customize it how you want it!",
