   "meta": {
    "application": "BambuStudio-02.06.00.51",
    "profile_title": "Articulated Stingray - Multi-Color Optimized",
    "profile_notes": "This profile has been meticulously fine-tuned specifically for this articulated multi-color model. The default settings have been adjusted to ensure the print-in-place hinges articulate freely right off the build plate, and the dual-color surface details remain crisp and clean. Key Optimization Changes: Wall Generator: Arachne (Changed from Classic) The Arachne engine dynamically adjusts line width during slicing. This produces cleaner perimeters around the intricate white spots and the delicate hinge mechanisms, eliminating tiny gaps and ensuring tighter surface details without over-extrusion. Order of Walls: Outer/Inner (Changed from Inner/Outer) Printing the outer wall first locks in the exact external dimensions of the model. This is essential for print-in-place articulated joints, ensuring the tolerances remain precise so the segments do not fuse together and can move freely immediately. Avoid Crossing Wall: Enabled (Changed from Disabled) Forcing the nozzle to travel within the boundaries of the printed parts rather than across empty space drastically reduces stringing. This prevents dark filament streaks from oozing and ruining the bright white spots on the stingray's back. Initial Layer Speed: Slower extrusion on the very first layer gives the filament more time to bond securely with the build plate. Articulated models have many small, disconnected first-layer footprints that are prone to detaching and failing if printed too quickly.",
